The bound is false at the requested physics standard, using the standard Bethe-ansatz/WZW identification.

The symmetric rank-two SU(8) chain has
\[
d=36,\qquad \|h\|=\frac32,\qquad c=\frac{63}{5},\qquad v=\frac{\pi}{4},
\]
so
\[
\frac{A}{2\pi\|h\|}=\frac{21}{20}>1.
\]
Local matrix checks and two thermal estimators support the normalization.

More strongly, symmetric rank-\(N\) SU(\(N\)) chains give
\[
\frac{A}{2\pi\|h\|}=\frac{N^2-1}{2NH_N}\longrightarrow\infty.
\]
Thus no finite dimension-independent constant repairs the conjecture.

The positive extension is \(A\leq\pi\|h\|\) for all quadratic Majorana/BdG chains, including pairing and the full coboundary minimization.

